Debian 13 update (2026-10-01)
----------------------------
See QUALIFICATION-DEBIAN13 for the native amd64/arm64 package qualification.
Ubuntu-only scope statements below describe the initial packaging checkpoint.

Debian/Ubuntu packaging for the xmlsec module
===========================================

The native module and its compiler metadata belong to qore-xmlsec-module.
HTML API reference, example test and public test certificates/keys belong to
qore-xmlsec-module-doc. Debhelper creates matching detached debug symbols.
The example keys are public fixtures and must never be used as real identities.

Build prerequisites and supported scope
--------------------------------------

Use an isolated native build environment containing the packaged Qore runtime
and libqore-dev, then install Build-Depends from debian/control. The current
qualification target is Ubuntu 26.04 amd64 with Qore 3.0 development packages.
Other releases and architectures need a matching SDK and native qualification.
Cross builds are rejected because Qore/qpp execute during the build.

Packages link distribution libxml2, XML Security Library and its OpenSSL backend;
no crypto or XML implementation is bundled. The separate Qore XML module is
needed only for the integration tests. Its private libxml2 does not export
libxml2 symbols; xmlsec uses the distribution shared library.

The build preserves distribution hardening flags. Native Qore modules resolve
Qore symbols at load time without linking libqore. debian/rules derives minimum
runtime and libqore SONAME dependencies from the installed SDK; dh_shlibdeps
supplies other shared libraries. The runtime package is not Multi-Arch: same
because it requires the native Qore interpreter. There are no AOT user modules
or dependency trailers; ordinary dh_strip is appropriate.

Source and binary builds
------------------------

Use a fresh version for every changed upload. This snapshot precedes version
1.0.1. From a clean committed checkout:

    version=1.0.1~git20260928.1
    mkdir -p ../xmlsec-package-work
    git archive --format=tar --prefix="qore-xmlsec-module-$version/" \
        HEAD -- . ':!debian' | xz > \
        "../xmlsec-package-work/qore-xmlsec-module_$version.orig.tar.xz"
    tar -xf "../xmlsec-package-work/qore-xmlsec-module_$version.orig.tar.xz" \
        -C ../xmlsec-package-work
    cp -a debian "../xmlsec-package-work/qore-xmlsec-module-$version/"
    cd "../xmlsec-package-work/qore-xmlsec-module-$version"
    dpkg-buildpackage -S -us -uc

Extract the .dsc with dpkg-source -x into a clean directory. With dependencies
preinstalled, build as an unprivileged user with networking disabled:

    dpkg-buildpackage -b -us -uc

Architecture-only builds (-B) do not need Doxygen. Architecture-independent
builds (-A) produce documentation. Both DEB_BUILD_OPTIONS=nodoc and
DEB_BUILD_PROFILES=nodoc suppress documentation; the profile also omits the doc
package. Do not use nocheck for qualification.

Qualification and publication
-----------------------------

The upstream suite covers XML signatures/verification, XML and binary
encryption/decryption, key management, named arguments, invalid input and
concurrent operations. A module preflight requires the XML integration
dependency during package qualification; standalone source runs explicitly
skip when that optional external module is unavailable.

Installed fixtures run away from checkout/build paths. A fresh qcc executable
uses installed native class metadata, named constructors/methods, generated
session keys and key managers. No external services or real credentials are
needed. The minimal runtime must work without the SDK or Qore XML module.

Check source/binary Lintian, debug symbols, hardening, installation without the
SDK, documentation/debug coinstallation, dpkg -V, purge/reinstall and
reproducibility from different build directories/parallelism settings.
Retain source/package hashes, dependency versions, audit and test logs.
Testing PPA publication is separate from approval for a final general release.
